-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. HOW THE TERMS APPLY TO SELF-HOSTED DEPLOYMENTS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Terms were written mainly for products that Parabol hosts. For the
Software deployed under this License:

  (a) Source access and modification. Sections 4.1(i) and 4.1(ii) of the
      Terms do not prohibit anything that Section 2 or Section 3 of this
      License permits.

  (b) Operations. Licensee, not Parabol, operates Licensee Infrastructure.
      Uptime commitments, service credits, hosting, and backup obligations in
      Section 2 (Support and Service Levels) of the Terms or in any Order Form
      do not apply unless the Self-Hosted Order Form expressly says otherwise.
      Support commitments stated in the Self-Hosted Order Form still apply.

  (c) Customer Data. Customer Data stays on Licensee Infrastructure. Parabol
      receives Customer Data only if Licensee sends it, for example in a
      support request or through integrations, telemetry, or AI features that
      Licensee chooses to enable. Section 5 of the Terms applies to any
      Customer Data that Parabol does receive. Licensee is responsible for
      securing and backing up data on Licensee Infrastructure and for
      complying with laws that apply to it. Section 7.3 of the Terms (account
      deactivation and deletion) does not apply to data on Licensee
      Infrastructure.

  (d) Third-party services. Any service that Licensee connects to the
      Software (for example, an identity provider, AI model provider, email
      service, or integration) is a Third Party Service under Section 8 of the
      Terms.

  (e) Parabol Products. References in the Terms to the "Parabol Products" and
      the "Software" include the Software as licensed under this License.

